  "scope_limits": [
    "Finite review and tests do not prove absence of every bug.",
    "P08 service qualification is the declared q35/TCG single-CPU, 2GiB, modern VirtIO profile. Earlier SMP/protection diagnostics remain separate regressions; concurrent service storage on SMP and physical hardware are unqualified.",
    "The platform intentionally has bounded process/thread/handle/object/connection/heap and storage capacities. These are reviewed prototype limits, not production-scale service availability claims.",
    "Development authentication uses kernel-issued single-use LogonPermit capabilities for provisioned UIDs1001/1002. Password authentication and usable entropy bytes remain unavailable; no custom hash or deterministic token is counted as an implemented provider.",
    "N0, N1 alloc and bounded N2-foundation adapters are qualified separately. A maintained native Rust std port, arbitrary hosted crates and a complete POSIX environment are not claimed.",
    "One protected service owns the shared journaled ext2 development subset. CRC32 is not hostile-media authentication or rollback protection, and emulated flush cannot establish physical-drive power-loss behavior.",
    "The console is a functional native text surface. GUI composition, full typography, desktop fidelity and the P00-P10/P11-P15 integration milestones remain later phases.",
    "C03/C04 interleaving models establish the reviewed ownership/order invariants; they do not exhaustively schedule every machine instruction on hardware. Raw hashes identify bytes in the trusted local workspace rather than providing external attestation."
  ],
